The &#8216;cringe&#8217; drink from the 90s and 00s is officially back! (Picture: Getty Images/iStockphoto)



Here’s&nbsp;a riddle for you…&nbsp;

What&nbsp;is&nbsp;cringe-inducing&nbsp;and looks like the contents of a glowstick&nbsp;from a&nbsp;90s&nbsp;rave?&nbsp;&nbsp;

The Appletini, of course.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Yes, the&nbsp;cocktail&nbsp;that resembles the&nbsp;pulsating&nbsp;radioactive waste in the&nbsp;opening&nbsp;credits of The Simpsons is making a comeback.&nbsp;&nbsp;

What is the Appletini?&nbsp;




		Be prepared to see it on the bar menu once more (Picture: Getty Images/iStockphoto)



Good question.&nbsp;For the love of all things green&nbsp;and sour, what is the Appletini?&nbsp;

Along with the Piña Colada and Mateus Rosé, the Appletini&nbsp;became&nbsp;a byword for&nbsp;collective cultural&nbsp;embarrassment&nbsp;in the 90s and 00s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

In its original form,&nbsp;the Appletini&nbsp;was neon green, tasted of&nbsp;fake&nbsp;apple-flavoured sweets, and you could guarantee that no actual&nbsp;fruits&nbsp;were&nbsp;harmed&nbsp;in the making of it.&nbsp;It was a&nbsp;toxic wasteland of&nbsp;sugar, artificial colouring, e-numbers,&nbsp;and alcohol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

It&nbsp;was&nbsp;the&nbsp;cocktail&nbsp;that made serious mixologists cringe, created in an LA bar called Lola’s in 1997. The inventor was a&nbsp;bartender&nbsp;named Adam&nbsp;Karston, who originally called it ‘Adam’s Apple’&nbsp;but the name never stuck, thankfully.&nbsp;&nbsp;

